# Work Progress

## Purpose

Keep a concise active log of completed or materially changed work for <strong>{{PROJECT_NAME}}</strong>. Record outcomes, evidence, limits, and useful handoff paths rather than raw transcripts or every intermediate action.

`CURRENT_TASKS.en.md` describes work that is planned or underway. This document records work that has completed or changed enough to affect how the project should be understood.

## Active delivery or method identity

- <strong>Current major version or working method:</strong> Unconfirmed during initialization.
- <strong>Lifecycle:</strong> `unconfirmed`.
- <strong>Evidence authority:</strong> `reference-only` until the active identity is confirmed.
- <strong>Validity boundary:</strong> Confirm from current project evidence before treating an entry as authoritative.

## {{DATE}} — Project-management record initialized

- <strong>Objective:</strong> Establish reusable bilingual project memory.
- <strong>Outcome:</strong> Created the neutral management structure and Dashboard inputs.
- <strong>Evidence:</strong> Initialization report and generated files.
- <strong>Limits:</strong> Project-specific implementation progress remains unconfirmed until inspected or confirmed by the user.

## Entry format

Add new entries newest first with these fields when they are useful:

- <strong>Objective:</strong> What the completed or materially changed work was meant to accomplish.
- <strong>Change:</strong> The exact files, functions, or sections modified, reconciled against the pre-change plan.
- <strong>Outcome:</strong> The confirmed result or current state.
- <strong>Evidence:</strong> Tests executed, files, commands, artifacts, or explicit user confirmation.
- <strong>Limits:</strong> What the evidence or test coverage does not establish.
- <strong>Handoff paths:</strong> Current files or artifacts needed to continue or review the work, plus any timely modularization suggestions when tight coupling risks collateral edits.
- <strong>Lifecycle and authority changes:</strong> Reclassifications caused by this work, including replacements and validity boundaries.

## Maintenance

- Append after completed work or a material change that future work needs to understand.
- Keep entries concise and link to retained evidence instead of copying large output.
- Keep volatile counts, run state, and execution snapshots in dated entries. Copy only stable conclusions into goal, constraint, or current-state documents.
- Update `CURRENT_TASKS.en.md` for forward-looking status and `CURRENT_VERSION.en.md` for current behavior.
- When a major delivery version or working method changes and older detail would mislead normal work, move the superseded detailed body into a dated folder under `99_archive`, leave a concise restoration pointer here, and keep the archived material intact.
